---
import PlaygroundShell from '../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Simulate it" hint="Several nodes make Snowflake-style ids at the same moment. Choose how the 63 usable bits are split, then break things: share a machine id, set a clock back, or ask for more ids than one millisecond can hold.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Press <b>Reset</b>, then <b>Generate ids</b> twice. Each of the 2 nodes asks for 100 ids per round, so 400 ids are issued and 0 are duplicates: different machine ids keep the nodes apart even in the same millisecond.</li>
    <li>Press <b>Reset</b>, tick <b>Nodes 1 and 2 share machine id 1</b>, then press <b>Generate ids</b>: 200 ids are issued but only 100 are distinct, so 100 are duplicates. Same millisecond, same machine id and same sequence number give the same id.</li>
    <li>Press <b>Reset</b>, set <b>IDs requested per node</b> to 5,000 and press <b>Generate ids</b>. With <b>Sequence runs out</b> on "Wait for the next millisecond", 10,000 ids are issued with 0 duplicates, because each node waits 1 ms after its 4,096th id. Now press <b>Reset</b>, set <b>IDs requested per node</b> to 5,000 and <b>Sequence runs out</b> to "Wrap to 0 and carry on", and press <b>Generate ids</b>: 1,808 duplicates.</li>
    <li>Press <b>Reset</b>, set <b>Bit layout</b> to "14 machine bits, 8 sequence bits" and <b>IDs requested per node</b> to 5,000, then press <b>Generate ids</b>. Each node can make only 256 ids per millisecond, so each waits 19 ms (38 ms in total). More machine bits allow more machines but fewer ids per machine per millisecond.</li>
    <li>Press <b>Reset</b>, press <b>Generate ids</b> twice, press <b>Set node 1's clock back 2 ms</b>, then press <b>Generate ids</b> again. With <b>Clock moves back</b> on "Trust the clock", 600 ids are issued and 100 are duplicates, because node 1 reused a millisecond it had already used. Repeat from <b>Reset</b> with <b>Clock moves back</b> set to "Refuse to issue ids": 500 ids are issued, 0 duplicates and 1 refusal. With "Wait until it catches up": 600 ids, 0 duplicates, and node 1 waits 1 ms.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg uid" data-uid>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Bit layout
        <select class="pg-in" data-layout>
          <option value="10" selected>10 machine bits, 12 sequence bits</option>
          <option value="14">14 machine bits, 8 sequence bits</option>
          <option value="6">6 machine bits, 16 sequence bits</option>
        </select>
      </label>
      <label>Nodes
        <select class="pg-in" data-nodes>
          <option value="2" selected>2 nodes</option>
          <option value="3">3 nodes</option>
          <option value="4">4 nodes</option>
        </select>
      </label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" data-share /> Nodes 1 and 2 share machine id 1</label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>IDs requested per node
        <select class="pg-in" data-burst>
          <option value="100" selected>100 per round</option>
          <option value="300">300 per round</option>
          <option value="4096">4,096 per round</option>
          <option value="5000">5,000 per round</option>
        </select>
      </label>
      <label>Sequence runs out
        <select class="pg-in" data-overflow>
          <option value="wait" selected>Wait for the next millisecond</option>
          <option value="wrap">Wrap to 0 and carry on</option>
        </select>
      </label>
      <label>Clock moves back
        <select class="pg-in" data-clockpolicy>
          <option value="trust" selected>Trust the clock</option>
          <option value="refuse">Refuse to issue ids</option>
          <option value="wait">Wait until it catches up</option>
        </select>
      </label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <button class="btn pg-primary" type="button" data-generate>Generate ids</button>
      <button class="btn" type="button" data-rollback>Set node 1's clock back 2 ms</button>
      <button class="btn" type="button" data-reset>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="uid-bar" role="img" data-bar>
        <span class="uid-seg" style="--c: var(--muted); flex: 1">1</span>
        <span class="uid-seg" style="--c: var(--role-1); flex: 41">41</span>
        <span class="uid-seg" style="--c: var(--role-2)" data-machseg></span>
        <span class="uid-seg" style="--c: var(--role-3)" data-seqseg></span>
      </div>
      <p class="pg-note" data-layoutnote></p>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-note" data-clocknote></p>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-1)"><h3>Ids issued</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-issued></span><span class="pg-note" data-issuednote></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-dupbox style="--c: var(--role-3)"><h3>Duplicate ids</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-dups></span><span class="pg-note" data-dupsnote></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-4)"><h3>Waiting and refusals</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-waits></span><span class="pg-note" data-waitsnote></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-2)"><h3>Went backwards</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-back></span><span class="pg-note" data-backnote></span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <div>
      <h4>First and last id of the latest round</h4>
      <ul class="uid-ids pg-mono" data-ids></ul>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-note">Model: the clock starts at 1,000 ms after the generators' custom start date, and after each round it moves on to the millisecond after the last one any node used. Each id is time, then machine id, then sequence, so its value is time times 2 to the power of (machine bits + sequence bits), plus machine id times 2 to the power of the sequence bits, plus the sequence. The 41 time bits last 2 to the power of 41 ms, about 69.7 years. A duplicate is an id equal to one already issued in this run. "Went backwards" counts ids smaller than the previous id from the same node. Changing the layout, node count or shared machine id starts the run over. The run stops at 200,000 ids.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  type ClockPolicy = 'trust' | 'refuse' | 'wait';
  type Overflow = 'wait' | 'wrap';
  interface NodeState { machine: number; last: number; seq: number; prev: number | null; first: Row | null; end: Row | null }
  interface Row { id: number; time: number; machine: number; seq: number }
  interface Opts { machineBits: number; seqBits: number; nodes: number; share: boolean; burst: number; overflow: Overflow; clockPolicy: ClockPolicy }
  interface Run { clock: number; skew: number; round: number; issued: number; dups: number; waitMs: number; refused: number; back: number; seen: Set<number>; nodes: NodeState[] }
  interface Outcome { issued: number; dups: number; waitMs: number; refusedNodes: number[]; waitedNodes: number[]; stopped: boolean }

  // core:start
  const START_MS = 1000; const SKEW_STEP_MS = 2; const MAX_IDS = 200000; const TOTAL_BITS = 22; const TIME_BITS = 41;
  const MS_PER_YEAR = 1000 * 60 * 60 * 24 * 365.25;

  function newRun(o: Opts): Run {
    const nodes: NodeState[] = [];
    for (let i = 0; i < o.nodes; i++) nodes.push({ machine: i === 1 && o.share ? 1 : i + 1, last: -1, seq: 0, prev: null, first: null, end: null });
    return { clock: START_MS, skew: 0, round: 0, issued: 0, dups: 0, waitMs: 0, refused: 0, back: 0, seen: new Set(), nodes };
  }

  // One round: every node asks for `burst` ids at its own clock reading (node 1's clock may be set back by `skew`).
  function generate(run: Run, o: Opts): Outcome {
    const out: Outcome = { issued: 0, dups: 0, waitMs: 0, refusedNodes: [], waitedNodes: [], stopped: false };
    if (run.issued + o.nodes * o.burst > MAX_IDS) { out.stopped = true; return out; }
    const maxSeq = 2 ** o.seqBits - 1; const timeScale = 2 ** (o.machineBits + o.seqBits);
    run.round++;
    let nextClock = run.clock;
    run.nodes.forEach((n, i) => {
      const offset = i === 0 ? -run.skew : 0;
      let c = run.clock + offset; let nodeWait = 0; n.first = null; n.end = null;
      for (let k = 0; k < o.burst; k++) {
        if (c < n.last) {
          if (o.clockPolicy === 'refuse') { out.refusedNodes.push(i); run.refused++; break; }
          if (o.clockPolicy === 'wait') { nodeWait += n.last - c; c = n.last; }
        }
        if (c === n.last) {
          n.seq = (n.seq + 1) & maxSeq;
          if (n.seq === 0 && o.overflow === 'wait') { c += 1; nodeWait += 1; }
        } else n.seq = 0;
        n.last = c;
        const id = c * timeScale + n.machine * 2 ** o.seqBits + n.seq;
        const row: Row = { id, time: c, machine: n.machine, seq: n.seq };
        if (run.seen.has(id)) { out.dups++; run.dups++; } else run.seen.add(id);
        if (n.prev !== null && id < n.prev) run.back++;
        n.prev = id; out.issued++; run.issued++;
        if (!n.first) n.first = row;
        n.end = row;
      }
      if (nodeWait) { out.waitMs += nodeWait; out.waitedNodes.push(i); run.waitMs += nodeWait; }
      nextClock = Math.max(nextClock, c - offset);
    });
    run.clock = nextClock + 1;
    return out;
  }
  // core:end

  const DEFAULTS = { layout: '10', nodes: '2', share: false, burst: '100', overflow: 'wait', clockPolicy: 'trust' };
  const fmt = (n: number) => n.toLocaleString('en-US');
  const plural = (n: number, w: string) => `${fmt(n)} ${w}${n === 1 ? '' : 's'}`;
  const list = (xs: number[]) => xs.map((i) => `node ${i + 1}`).join(', ');

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-uid]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = <T extends Element>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s)!;
    const sel = (s: string) => q<HTMLSelectElement>(s);
    const opts = (): Opts => {
      const machineBits = Number(sel('[data-layout]').value);
      return { machineBits, seqBits: TOTAL_BITS - machineBits, nodes: Number(sel('[data-nodes]').value), share: q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-share]').checked,
        burst: Number(sel('[data-burst]').value), overflow: sel('[data-overflow]').value as Overflow, clockPolicy: sel('[data-clockpolicy]').value as ClockPolicy };
    };
    let run = newRun(opts());
    let last: Outcome | null = null;

    function renderLayout(o: Opts) {
      const m = q<HTMLElement>('[data-machseg]'); const s = q<HTMLElement>('[data-seqseg]');
      m.style.flex = String(o.machineBits); m.textContent = String(o.machineBits);
      s.style.flex = String(o.seqBits); s.textContent = String(o.seqBits);
      const years = (2 ** TIME_BITS / MS_PER_YEAR).toFixed(1);
      q('[data-layoutnote]').textContent = `1 sign bit (always 0), ${TIME_BITS} time bits (${years} years of milliseconds), ${o.machineBits} machine bits (up to ${fmt(2 ** o.machineBits)} machines), ${o.seqBits} sequence bits (up to ${fmt(2 ** o.seqBits)} ids per millisecond from each machine).`;
      q('[data-bar]').setAttribute('aria-label', `Layout of a 64-bit id: 1 sign bit, ${TIME_BITS} time bits, ${o.machineBits} machine bits, ${o.seqBits} sequence bits.`);
    }

    function render(message: string, bad: boolean) {
      const o = opts(); renderLayout(o);
      const distinct = run.seen.size;
      q('[data-clocknote]').textContent = `Clock: ${fmt(run.clock)} ms. Round ${run.round}. ${run.skew ? `Node 1's clock is set back ${run.skew} ms.` : 'Node 1\'s clock is correct.'} Machine ids: ${run.nodes.map((n, i) => `node ${i + 1} is ${n.machine}`).join(', ')}.`;
      q('[data-issued]').textContent = fmt(run.issued);
      q('[data-issuednote]').textContent = `${fmt(distinct)} distinct`;
      q('[data-dups]').textContent = fmt(run.dups);
      q('[data-dupsnote]').textContent = run.dups ? 'two records would get the same key' : 'every id so far is unique';
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-dupbox]').style.setProperty('--c', run.dups ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--role-3)');
      q('[data-waits]').textContent = `${fmt(run.waitMs)} ms, ${plural(run.refused, 'refusal')}`;
      q('[data-waitsnote]').textContent = 'waiting added up over all nodes, and refused requests';
      q('[data-back]').textContent = fmt(run.back);
      q('[data-backnote]').textContent = run.back ? 'ids smaller than the node\'s previous id' : 'each node\'s ids only grow';
      const v = q('[data-verdict]'); v.textContent = message; v.classList.toggle('bad', bad);
      const ul = q('[data-ids]'); ul.textContent = '';
      run.nodes.forEach((n, i) => {
        if (!n.first || !n.end) return;
        const rows: [string, Row][] = n.first.id === n.end.id ? [['only', n.first]] : [['first', n.first], ['last', n.end]];
        for (const [name, r] of rows) {
          const li = document.createElement('li');
          li.textContent = `Node ${i + 1}, ${name}: ${r.id} = time ${fmt(r.time)}, machine ${r.machine}, sequence ${fmt(r.seq)}`;
          ul.append(li);
        }
      });
      if (!ul.children.length) { const li = document.createElement('li'); li.textContent = 'No ids yet. Press Generate ids.'; ul.append(li); }
    }

    function restart(message: string) { run = newRun(opts()); last = null; render(message, false); }

    q('[data-generate]').addEventListener('click', () => {
      const o = opts(); const before = run.dups;
      last = generate(run, o);
      if (last.stopped) { render('The run is at its limit of 200,000 ids. Press Reset to start again.', false); return; }
      const parts = [`Round ${run.round}: ${plural(last.issued, 'id')} issued, ${plural(run.dups - before, 'duplicate')}.`];
      if (last.refusedNodes.length) parts.push(`${list(last.refusedNodes)} refused to issue ids because its clock is behind its last id.`);
      if (last.waitedNodes.length) parts.push(`${list(last.waitedNodes)} waited ${fmt(last.waitMs)} ms in total, so no millisecond was reused.`);
      if (run.dups - before && o.overflow === 'wrap' && o.burst > 2 ** o.seqBits) parts.push(`The sequence wrapped to 0 inside the same millisecond, which repeats ids.`);
      else if (run.dups - before && run.nodes.some((n, i) => run.nodes.findIndex((m) => m.machine === n.machine) !== i)) parts.push('Two nodes use the same machine id.');
      else if (run.dups - before && run.skew) parts.push('Node 1 went back to a millisecond it had already used.');
      render(parts.join(' '), run.dups - before > 0);
    });
    q('[data-rollback]').addEventListener('click', () => {
      run.skew += SKEW_STEP_MS;
      render(`Node 1's clock now reads ${run.skew} ms earlier than it should, as after a time correction. The next round shows what each policy does.`, false);
    });
    q('[data-reset]').addEventListener('click', () => {
      sel('[data-layout]').value = DEFAULTS.layout; sel('[data-nodes]').value = DEFAULTS.nodes; q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-share]').checked = DEFAULTS.share;
      sel('[data-burst]').value = DEFAULTS.burst; sel('[data-overflow]').value = DEFAULTS.overflow; sel('[data-clockpolicy]').value = DEFAULTS.clockPolicy;
      restart('Reset: the clock is at 1,000 ms and no ids have been issued.');
    });
    ['[data-layout]', '[data-nodes]', '[data-share]'].forEach((s) => q(s).addEventListener('change', () => restart('Settings changed, so the run started over.')));
    ['[data-burst]', '[data-overflow]', '[data-clockpolicy]'].forEach((s) => q(s).addEventListener('change', () => render('Setting changed. Press Generate ids to run a round with it.', false)));
    render('Press Generate ids to start.', false);
  });
</script>
<style is:global>
  .playground .uid-bar { display: flex; gap: 2px; width: 100%; }
  .playground .uid-seg { min-width: 0; text-align: center; padding: 6px 0; border-radius: 4px; font: 600 .8rem var(--font-mono); color: var(--text); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--c) 24%, var(--surface)); border: 1px solid var(--c); }
  .playground .uid-ids { list-style: none; margin: 6px 0 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 4px; }
  .playground .uid-ids li { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
</style>
